IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Curative Petition (C) No. 44 of 2023
CITATION: 2023 SCC OnLine SC 1666
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: D.Y. Chandrachud, S.K. Kaul, Sanjiv Khanna, B.R. Gavai, Surya Kant, et al.

PARTIES:
Curative Bench Seven Judges

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Stamp Act, 1899, Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 35 Stamp Act, Section 11(6A) Arbitration Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
unstamped agreement, competence competence, referral stage, seven judge bench

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Seven-judge bench unanimously held that non-stamping or insufficient stamping of an underlying commercial contract does not render the arbitration clause void ab initio at referral stage.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 35 Stamp Act, Section 11(6A) Arbitration Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

